<title>USA: U.S. opens agricultural affairs office in Hanoi.</title>
<headline>U.S. opens agricultural affairs office in Hanoi.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States opened an agricultural affairs office in Hanoi on Thursday, the Agriculture Department announced, describing an upsurge in farm trade with Vietnam.</p>
<p>About $36 million in U.S. farm products were shipped to Vietnam in fiscal 1996, mostly cotton and corn. Vietnam sent $190 million in goods to U.S. buyers in the same period, three-quarters of it coffee.</p>
<p>&quot;The U.S. Agriculture Department is committed to helping Vietnam develop as a potential trading partner,&quot; said Tim Galvin, deputy administrator of the department's Foreign Agricultural Service.</p>
<p>Ross Kreamer is agricultural attache in the office, located in the U.S. embassy.</p>
<p>The United States and Vietnam normalised relations in July 1995.</p>
</text>
